# Physics 3D

Physics workload measurement admits frames by their start time and retains the complete last frame even when it overruns the requested duration. Never censor a slow crossing frame from latency gates. Record the overrun and worst observed frame separately. `physics-stress` can activate, replace and unload a door source through shared geometry quarantine/publication, then capture paired physics/navigation/entity/projectile state for a fresh-process restart. Stable shape IDs and host route-direction/projectile generations survive recovery; runtime handles do not. Checkpoint capture/write and restart startup are separate measurements. Elapsed runtime alone never passes the two-hour churn/restart gate.

Optional `MotionPolicyWorld.SetMotionPolicy` changes mode and complete controller policy atomically, with mandatory `VelocityRetain`/`VelocityClear`. Validate current pose, geometry and retained momentum before mutation; preserve body/collider/joint handles, authored mass/locks, ownership, forces and activation. Reject dynamic concave geometry, incompatible upright controllers and nonzero retained velocity for Static/ExternalPose. Root `SetPhysicsMotionPolicy` synchronizes bindings and invalidates previous trajectory generations only on success; queued policies fence attachment identity and intervening policy changes. Checkpoints capture the resulting policy/intent, not transition tokens. Accepted contacts affected by native type changes are geometrically revalidated with zero invented force; continuous replay retains fractional separation/reentry, and rejection cannot publish its tracker. Exact tangent rotational intervals currently retain an explicit nonconvergence regression pending correction; never treat unresolved intervals as clear.

Portable source preparation v2 requires an explicit `Settings.CharacterPolicy` before authored Unity CharacterController metadata becomes server movement. `GolemKinematicCharacters` maps step/slope/skin onto caller-supplied controller support/work budgets, with default gravity disabled; dimensions remain collider-owned. Nonzero movement deadband, disabled collision/recovery and incompatible compound/tilted geometry produce preflight diagnostics. Preserve the raw authoring metadata, hash the full conversion policy, and never silently load a character as an ordinary kinematic body.

Server-owned `StartPhysicsTrajectory`/`CancelPhysicsTrajectory` provide copied, bounded multi-tick scripted/external anchor poses with polling state and fresh generation tokens. Timed body-origin pose segments retain shortest-arc rotations in the same shared solver time; they cannot be mixed with navigation segments. Non-nav users work independently without a navigation service; when navigation exists, capture the chosen profile's quarantine before simulation. Pause time while unsafe, retain actual blocked body poses, and never undo transferred momentum on cancellation. ExternalPose rejects autonomous nonzero velocities; its last reported velocity can be checkpointed but moving again requires admitted timed intent. Explicit teleport remains final-placement-only and cancels active intent. Box3D pose trajectories currently require continuous motion and convex/compound geometry; concave bodies and rotating upright controllers fail admission explicitly. Active serializable trajectories survive paired checkpoints with fresh cancellation tokens; game callbacks/authority rules are not persisted.

Contact history is transactional with frame acceptance. Simulate updates a private
tracker; rejection/fault discards it. `ShutdownWorld.CloseWithEvents` returns only
terminal accepted pairs and queued lifecycle cleanup, closes mutation first, and
is idempotent. Server shutdown dispatches copied events without accepting new commands.

`DebugWorld.CaptureDebug` is an explicit owner-goroutine diagnostic seam outside active simulation. It copies accepted state and exact native body-local collider leaves with bounded geometry/annotation budgets and omission counts. Fault/pending native poses are separately flagged and never imply acceptance. Caller-supplied frame events, paths, queries and navigation targets are bounded copies; no always-on logging is added to the production loop. `box3d/cmd/physics-debug` emits a real sample capture and verifies the shared Unity fixture. `physics-stress -debug-capture` writes bounded failed-frame captures only when selected. Debug JSON is visualization data, not portable source or recovery state.

Optional portable `PlacementValidator` checks complete solid volumes without changing pose or momentum. Query truncation/unsupported geometry cannot imply clearance. Body attachment and explicit teleport/external-pose admission require this capability; zero tolerance rejects penetration independently of solver contact slop. Backend motion-admission rejection is distinct from a failed world frame: report the rejected intent plus every actual solver path so root runtime can discard only its proposed metadata while accepting interacting physical results.

Portable `CheckpointWorld` recovery captures accepted poses, velocities, activation, joint descriptions and unconsumed forces under stable content IDs. Never serialize backend handles or contact caches. `PrepareRestore` builds an isolated world and rejects commitment after any target mutation; successful commitment changes world identity so every old handle becomes stale. Restore contact classification is `RestoredContact`, not ordinary `Enter`. This reconstructs valid physical state without promising bitwise solver continuation. Root paired entity/navigation recovery and manifest publication remain separate from the backend.

Content leases capture source/settings/fingerprint identity and rebind through `ContentLookup` only after a paired world restore. `ContentIDs` exposes owned identity lists without copying large geometry; reject overlapping ownership. Implicit world-joint anchors are scoped by source fingerprint. `Prepared.Bounds` uses authored geometry; `Instance.Bounds` uses current accepted poses, including disabled geometry, for complete old/new quarantine checks. Neither includes navigation bake clearance; the host must add that influence.

`golem/physics3d` is a separate Go module without root runtime imports. It owns portable descriptions, identity, validation, query and explicit-frame contracts. `golem/physics3d/box3d` is a separate module using Go 1.27.1 and the pure-Go Box3D solver. Root server attachment and navigation coordination belong in `golem`, never the backend or portable content loader. Test these modules explicitly; root `./...` excludes them.

Authoritative positions and wire positions remain float32. Validate finite poses and the supported ±4,096 metre envelope. Keep gameplay/navigation anchors distinct from body origins and centres of mass. Legacy collision3d, 2D backends and footprint v1 retain their existing semantics.

Queries distinguish initial overlap, touching, penetration, solid and sensor roles. Results retain exact generational collider/subshape identity and optional entity owner. Caller buffers must report truncation; full buffers are never proof of clearance. Mutations require an explicit synchronization boundary before queries. Keep source geometry and backend acceleration data separate, and reject malformed or unsupported content without substituting bounding boxes.

`QueryBatch` only parallelizes independent read-only work within a tick-owned call, joins every worker before returning and validates all inputs before dispatch. Per-query output buffers cannot overlap. Keep metrics accounting on the owner goroutine. Owner contact aggregation is opt-in and maintains generational child-pair counts at frame/fraction boundaries; restoration emits `RestoredContact`, never an ordinary entry phase.

`physics3d/content` owns strict bounded Scribe source decoding, immutable `Prepared` captures, explicit solver-margin/CCD policy hashes, owner resolution and rollback of only newly constructed handles. It has no runtime/server or backend imports. Unsupported authored joint/material controls remain inspectable diagnostics and prevent loading; never silently drop them. `physics3d/box3d` cooks private hull/BVH leaves before registering reusable shapes. Native image artifacts include format/settings/source/fork identities and are separate from portable source; an empty source snapshot hash is not release evidence. Nonidentity local mesh poses must transform and recook the instance geometry. Source identity lookup survives neither removal nor an incomplete rollback.

Simulation is tick-owned and staged: validate proposals before solving, freeze mutations through the frame, integrate fixed substeps once, then accept all body/entity state or fault the whole world. Never restore one pushed character after impulses have affected other bodies. Driven characters apply bounded tangential forces once per substep; the solver owns contact transfer. No extra push impulses, proxy bodies or unsupported vertical hovering.

Optional `BodyDesc.Controller` owns a single upright solid capsule. Dimensions come from geometry; nonzero angular velocity and tilted capsules fail admission. Kinematic/scripted movement retains every swept step/slide phase and timed navigation corner. Driven mode keeps finite mass and requires zero synthetic step height; physical stair ascent depends on actual contact response. `SetCharacterVelocity`/server `SetPhysicsControllerVelocity` retain intent, overridden by explicit frame navigation. Exact support collider/body generations and features are re-probed; local support points belong to body origins, not COM. Support transport spans locomotion phases, bounds angular travel, and sweeps passengers under ceilings. Relative kinematic obstruction clips the participants before integration; dynamic contact transfer remains solver-owned. Checkpoints preserve controller intent/fall speed but rebuild support identities. Additional shared intervals and solver microsteps never recompute bounded drive force or multiply elapsed time; report interval/microstep/candidate/refinement counts separately. Actual-server correctness fixtures do not establish full-load capacity.

With continuous simulation enabled, the Box3D adapter admits relative translations and rotations through bounded internal microsteps, then validates actual solver paths. Defaults retain four outer substeps, a 1/240-second maximum internal delta and four/two velocity/relaxation passes at each time boundary; Config/checkpoints retain these choices. Preserve force/torque duration and every microstep's body-origin pose, anchor, fraction and contact transition. Count the final relaxed impulse once, and sum manifold-point impulses into collider-pair forces before owner aggregation. Report actual microstep/candidate/path-refinement counts; limits, unresolved casts and unsafe joint-generated paths fault the whole frame. Fresh geometric refinement separates conservative path bounds from actual penetration. Query tolerances remain independent of the 10mm solver penetration policy and its 1-micrometre float32 classification allowance. Kinematic triangle meshes require this path; dynamic concave geometry remains unsupported. Triangle winding still controls solver response, and unresolved passenger crushing needs host transport policy rather than individual-body rewinds.

`CastColliderMotion` and `QueryColliderMotion` use existing persistent geometry and supplied BODY trajectories. Sweep bounds include full rotational arcs; static candidates come from the backend tree and supplied moving targets are tested against swept bounds. Pair normals point A-to-B, world-query normals target-to-query. Earliest hits do not define complete concave sensor exit/re-entry intervals. Never infer a union MTD from a leaf penetration or omit numerical failure/overflow from clearance decisions.

`ColliderMotionIntervals` unions all convex-leaf intervals, preserving translational/rotational exit and re-entry across compounds and meshes. Rotation uses conservative support-plane separation and inner-Minkowski overlap certificates; boundary brackets stay within the requested distance tolerance. Its bounded work and output capacity must fail explicitly on unresolved geometry. Continuous sensors use 10-micrometre boundary tolerance and replay private pending contact state in fraction order after the backend unlocks, retaining all intermediate endpoints and accepted-only cleanup. Query-only geometry is not a physical sensor participant. Sensor-free worlds keep immediate contact observation; no sensor workload capacity is implied by focused correctness checks.

Real-terrain sphere sweeps use analytic triangle features to avoid GJK fraction stalls. Validate exact authored float32 source/query inputs against an independent analytic reference as well as Unity. `qualification/physics/analyze_sphere_witness.py` is offline reference math only; it never changes production precision. Retain strict Unity mismatch records separately when rounded world witnesses differ from geometric normals or analytic distances. Do not alter production normals or relax accuracy thresholds to manufacture reference parity.

New physics execution artifacts, Unity projects, caches, temporary files and qualification evidence belong under `D:/Demiurgos/tests/physics-validation`. Preserve completed runs and existing navigation evidence. Record exact source snapshots and distinguish local fork checks from published dependency resolution. Missing, unsupported or unmeasured release gates are failures to qualify; an early vertical slice is not workstream completion.

`examples/physics-stress` is a separate actual-server consumer. Full mode fixes 1,000 moving staged-navigation characters, 1,000 awake dynamic bodies, 500 swept projectile states, 100,000 static collider instances, five million unique resident mesh triangles and 10,000 additional mixed queries per tick. Correctness and rehearsal modes are explicitly reduced diagnostics. Count actual reconciled displacement, route modes, scheduled movement, awake bodies, query/projectile cadence and complete measurement windows. Percentile bucket values are upper bounds; report omissions, startup and allocations separately. Its synthetic plane is additional combined-load coverage, never a substitute for existing navigation terrain/multilevel/construction/churn/restart or representative-content gates. `qualification/Run-PhysicsStress.ps1` stages exact engine/fork/navigation sources and runs only from preserved validation-workspace copies. Do not overlap timed workloads with unrelated heavy tests. The user-selected physics platform scope is Windows AMD64 and native Linux AMD64. On 2026-11-12 the user explicitly excluded ARM64 if navigation had not used a native ARM64 runner; retained navigation evidence confirms ARM64 compilation only and unexecuted hosted CI. Preserve that audit and the decision in the requirements manifest; do not report ARM64 as either passed or a remaining physics gate.

Library changes belong in `C:/Demiurgos/box3d-go`, with upstream attribution, focused regression coverage and a patch ledger. Preserve upstream cast semantics; Golem's initial-overlap policy belongs in the adapter. No native fallback or float64 migration is authorized. Local workspace/replace overrides remain uncommitted.

The stress runner's explicit `-SIMD` option selects the existing pure-Go Box3D `box3d_simd` build with `GOEXPERIMENT=simd`. Record experiment, build tags, target CPU capability and exact toolchain alongside results; scalar runs clear an inherited experiment. SIMD is an opt-in candidate configuration, not a silent production default or proof of support on CPUs without AVX. Worker tuning preserves all required workload counts. Native Linux execution in WSL uses a Linux Go executable and Linux binary; record the virtualization environment. A cross-build or emulated ARM64 run never substitutes for a native ARM64 host.
